fun main() {
  for (var i = 0; i < 2; i = i + 1) {
    var i = 99;
    print i;
  }
}
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// w08_shadow.mini  (PDF section 8, saved there as shadow.mini)
// a body-local i shadows the counter. This is the version WITHOUT the
// rounds safety counter that inputs/shadow.mini has.
//
// Try:  minic lower w08/w08_shadow.mini -> the (block (var i 99) (print i))
//         stays nested, and (assign i ...) comes after it
//       minic run   w08/w08_shadow.mini -> 99
//                                          99
//
// Before the edit: "internal: TODO WEEK08 ...", exit 70.
//
// The update i = i + 1 sits outside the original body block, so it binds to
// the header i (0 -> 1 -> 2), not the inner i = 99. When I tested a broken
// version that spliced the body's children into the while body, the update
// bound to the inner i, the header i never changed, and this file printed 99
// forever (I had to stop it). inputs/shadow.mini stops after 3 because of
// rounds.
